-- title:
--   From HTo G G Hat Idx Meas Sum Is Some False Weight
-- statement:
--   **Left weighting preserves the residual G-hat partition.** Fix $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, let $S$ be a local operator, and write $U_{x,g}$ and $R_x$ for the indexed G-hat effects and incomplete-part total. The failure branch obeys
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{g\,:\,g.\mathrm{isSome}=\mathrm{false}}S\,U_{x,g}U_{x,g}=S\,R_x.
--   $$
--
--   This residual identity is used in the half-sandwich and Bernoulli-tail expansions.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
